    "corrected": {
      "ok": true,
      "value": {
        "status": "failed",
        "error": "OpenAlex returned a page whose meta carries no numeric count for 2024-06-10",
        "note": null,
        "record_count": 0,
        "cursors": [
          "*"
        ],
        "records": [],
        "progress": [],
        "params": [
          {
            "cursor": "*",
            "filter": "from_publication_date:2024-06-10,to_publication_date:2024-06-10",
            "mailto": "a@b.c",
            "per_page": 200
          }
        ]
      },
      "why": "Python accepts a boolean as a numeric count: `isinstance(True, int)` is True, so `promised` becomes the literal `True` and reaches a caller-facing message, while `False` records a promise of 0. The comment beside the check states the rule it fails to enforce, and `transparency.analyzer._json_count` excludes `bool` by name. The port applies that rule here.",
      "issue": 313
    }
